      "base_year": 2024,
      "producer": "microcosm build uk-frs-calibration-attempt-20260930T155755Z-f8182725 (tools/build_uk_rowwise_candidate.py --release-role national on microcosm main c5a1cba8, the PolicyEngine/microcosm#1045 merge, with policyengine-uk 2.100.0), staged 2026-09-30 in the Hugging Face dataset repo policyengine/populace-uk-private (commit 1b295f37); all seven calibration-seam gates passed, as did microcosm's evaluation against the Enhanced FRS; a staging build, not a certified release",
      "observation": "FRS 2024-25 spine; capital gains amounts redrawn from HMRC Table 3 (size of gain by taxable income, 2024-25) with asset types from HMRC Tables 7 and 8, gains qualifying for Business Asset Disposal Relief and Investors' Relief imputed from HMRC Table 4, and gain carriers conditioned on wealth through a mass-conserving support split (microcosm#1045); the sub-exempt remainder drawn from the Advani-Summers within-band distribution (microcosm#970); household weights calibrated to 1,090 targets for 2024-25, among them HMRC's CGT totals, size bands, age, region, gains by taxable income band (Table 3) and the BADR bands (Table 4)",
      "notes": "The build's projection gate (uk_cgt_projection_entrants, run on policyengine-uk 2.100.0) counts 6.7k gainers that uprating carries over the frozen exempt amount by 2030, against HMRC's 73k taxpayers with gains of \u00a33,000 to \u00a35,999 in 2024-25 (Table 2.1a); this repo's uprating audit counts 6.9k on policyengine-uk 2.104.0.",
      "columns": "It carries capital_gains, capital_gains_residential_property (the residential schedule) and capital_gains_badr (gains qualifying for Business Asset Disposal Relief or Investors' Relief), and no carried-interest column.",
